## Program Outcome

Tool Shed derives release baselines from a repository's bounded declared identity policy and
reachable exact Git history, never from a hidden universal formatting assumption. Campaigns whose
execution is wholly terminal but whose assignments are administratively stale can be reconciled
through one guarded atomic route into a truthful non-success terminal result. The complete behavior
is portable, documented, cross-platform qualified, released, production-verified, and recursively
reconciled.

